arket"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Simple Present Tense <br><br>You use the Simple Present tense to:<br><span class=\"bullet\">talk about a routine action or specific action that happens regularly</span> <br> <span class=\"bullet\">say a general truth</span><br> <span class=\"bullet\"> give personal information</span><br><br> You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Present Simple.<br><br>Present Continuous Tense <br><br>You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:<br><span class=\"bullet\">a current event or action happening around now  </span> <br><span class=\"bullet\">events that are going to happen soon (future plans)  </span> <br><br>You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We provide bus transportation from Waterloo station.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm thinking about going to Stonehenge.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We take you to the Roman town of Bath.</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Where are you staying?</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Great Britain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the country formed by England, Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Welcome to British Discoveries\u2026 the place to discover Great Britain!  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you go on an excursion to Stonehenge."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Stonehenge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an ancient monument in England"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm thinking about going to Stonehenge."}, {"type": "audio", "c